{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Larger breadboards, alligator clip leads, and photoresistors feel like natural next choices because they let me connect and experiment with the boards, wires, switches, and relays I have bought.",
    "The component tester fits my interest in building circuits because checking parts before connecting them would help with the same hands-on work."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Printer filament and fast-blinking LEDs assume projects I have not shown a need for; making electronic prototypes does not mean I need printed parts or decorative lighting effects.",
    "Banana leads require compatible sockets, the signal generator needs a specific testing purpose, and the lock nuts require a matching thread size. My purchases do not establish those needs."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My electronics purchases seem to have been taken as interest in almost any electronics accessory, even when it requires equipment or a purpose I have not mentioned.",
    "My LED kit and caster purchases seem to have been stretched into interest in lighting effects and particular hardware, although those details determine whether I can use the items."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The strongest connection across my electronics purchases is practical circuit assembly: useful recommendations should help me connect, check, or experiment with those components.",
    "Something can fit my interests without being a purchase I would make now. Calipers could help with a future fitting task, but I would wait until that task arises."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my interest in circuit prototyping but sometimes assumed equipment, compatibility, or project needs that my history does not establish."
}"}
